---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: 'How do I calculate my age on a cut-off date?', a: 'Enter your date of birth and the cut-off date from the notification. The tool counts complete years, then months, then days between them.' },
  { q: 'Is the cut-off date counted in my age?', a: 'The tool counts up to and including the cut-off date, so someone born on 1 January is exactly one year old on the next 1 January. Check how your notification words it.' },
  { q: 'What does "within completed years" mean?', a: 'It lets you stay eligible until the day before you complete one more year. For a limit of 27, that means up to 27 years 11 months 30 days. The other option stops at exactly 27 years.' },
  { q: 'Where do I enter age relaxation?', a: 'Type the extra years your notification allows for your category in the relaxation box. We do not list category rules, so take that number from the official notification.' },
  { q: 'Does it work for leap-year birthdays?', a: 'Yes. Months have their real number of days, and a 29 February birthday is treated as 1 March in non-leap years when checking limits.' },
];
---
<ToolLayout slug="age-calculator-for-cut-off-date" faqs={faqs}>
  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: lead paragraph, drafted by AI. */}
  <p slot="lead">
    Use this age calculator for a cut-off date to find your exact age in years, months and days on the date a
    notification names. Add the minimum and maximum age limits to see at once whether you are within them.
  </p>

  <div slot="tool" id="ag-tool">
    <div class="row two">
      <div class="field"><label for="ag-dob">Date of birth</label><input id="ag-dob" type="date" /></div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ag-cut">Cut-off date (age as on)</label>
        <input id="ag-cut" type="date" />
        <div class="chips"><button type="button" class="chip" id="ag-today">Use today</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <details>
      <summary>Check an age limit (optional)</summary>
      <div class="row three" style="margin-top:10px">
        <div class="field"><label for="ag-min">Minimum age (years)</label><input id="ag-min" type="number" min="0" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="ag-max">Maximum age (years)</label><input id="ag-max" type="number" min="0" inputmode="numeric" /></div>
        <div class="field"><label for="ag-relax">Relaxation (extra years)</label><input id="ag-relax" type="number" min="0" inputmode="numeric" value="0" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="ag-rule">How does the notification count the maximum?</label>
        <select id="ag-rule">
          <option value="exact">Not more than X years (exactly X years 0 months 0 days)</option>
          <option value="completed">Within X completed years (up to X years 11 months 30 days)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="result" aria-live="polite">
      <p class="label" style="margin:0">Your age on the cut-off date</p>
      <p class="big" id="ag-out">–</p>
      <p id="ag-detail" class="hint">Enter your date of birth and the cut-off date.</p>
      <div id="ag-elig"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* AUTHOR REVIEW: how-to and worked example drafted by AI. */}
  <h2>How to find your age on a cut-off date</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Select your date of birth.</li>
    <li>Select the "age as on" date given in the notification, or press "Use today" for your age now.</li>
    <li>Read the age in years, months and days. The total number of days is shown below it.</li>
    <li>If the notification gives an age range, open "Check an age limit" and enter the numbers to see the earliest and latest birth dates that qualify.</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p class="worked">
    Date of birth 15 May 2000 and cut-off date 1 January 2026. From 15 May 2000 to 15 May 2025 is 25 complete years.
    From 15 May to 15 December is 7 months, and from 15 December to 1 January is 17 days. The result is 25 years,
    7 months and 17 days. With a maximum age of 27, you are comfortably within the limit.
  </p>
  <h2>Before you rely on the result</h2>
  <p>
    Notifications word age rules in different ways, and relaxations depend on category. That is why this tool asks you
    for the numbers instead of guessing them. Read the official notification, apply the cut-off date it names, and use
    this calculator only to do the arithmetic.
  </p>
  <script>import '../../scripts/age.js';</script>
</ToolLayout>
